# Wire-schema compatibility repair

Evidence before mutation: provider-runtime-02/run-01-stdout.txt records status stopped, round investigator role_rejected, cleanup_complete true and zero candidates; stderr records BadRequestError HTTP400 with no error code/parameter. The controller confirms terminal session and preserved terminal verification. This establishes a rejected request, not a confirmed schema-keyword cause. The change is a compatibility repair hypothesis requiring independent review and separately authorized actual execution; it is not proof that the original 400 is fixed.

Scoped preimages of provider.py, agent_loop.py and the SDD preparation helper are preserved under originals/ with preimages.json. Exact changed hashes are in hashes.json and unified diff in change.patch. No evaluator closure file changed: contracts.py EVALUATOR_SOURCE_PATHS_V5 excludes all three, so no rebuild is required.

Shared wire_role_schema_v5 projects only recognized schema nodes, preserving canonical local schemas, RoleRequest IDs, schema authority hashes and parser/binding checks. It removes uniqueItems at schema nodes and root $schema/x-pit-optimizer-v5-authority, translates the current disjoint oneOf alternatives to anyOf, and translates current string const discriminants to string enum literals. It retains required/additionalProperties, all min/max constraints, and property names/data values—including the author property named default. Unsupported const forms and conflicting alternative declarations reject rather than guess. It never mutates the original schema mapping.

agent_loop.request_pit_optimizer_v5_json_once uses this projector for its actual response_format schema. The preparation helper uses the same projector, preserves initial-response-schema.json as canonical local authority, and additionally saves initial-wire-response-schema.json and its digest. Its review body now contains the actual projected schema. Messages, response handling, local schema validation, ledger and role retry behavior are unchanged.

prospective_role_usage_v5 takes max(canonical-schema bytes, projected-schema bytes), preserving conservative prior accounting. Actual archived campaign01 and campaign02 initial schemas/bodies were loaded unchanged for a pure local preflight: canonical2087bytes, projected1720bytes; old and new input bounds are exactly10305 for each. No invented inputs, role responses, calls or synthetic probes were used. Future schemas that grow under projection receive the larger bound.

The existing observational failure diagnostic additionally emits schema_keyword_hints from a fixed eight-keyword vocabulary. It derives matches internally from bounded error.message/error.param/metadata.raw strings; it never emits those strings, raw metadata, or arbitrary provider text. It does not change settlement and is marked accounting_authority false. The hints identify keyword mentions, not authenticated cause attribution.

Official source context supplied by controller: OpenAI structured outputs supports anyOf and required/additionalProperties; the Microsoft Azure-specific documented subset explicitly excludes uniqueItems. This is not a claim that Azure's full subset is universally identical to every OpenRouter route. No new network lookup occurred here.

Scoped Ruff and in-memory compile passed. No tests read/created/run; no external/provider/Docker calls, campaign launches, commits or hook changes. Frozen failed campaign histories are preserved; prepare a distinct reviewed body/manifest package before another separately authorized attempt.

Controller-requested additional actual author preflight: runtime-04 archived request 39acd001...2259e622bf (full path/hash in actual-author-projection.json) preserves its named default property and four disjoint literal branches. Existing oneOf branches become anyOf, each kind const becomes typed string enum; value schemas remain exactly equal and canonical source schema remains byte-identical. Canonical3264 versus wire3005 bytes. No synthetic schema or remote call. Source hashes unchanged by this preflight.
